    "math_academy_id": "q-124295",
    "knowledge_point_id": "dd51cf5a-ca8a-5f89-91d6-8f1a58412314",
    "knowledge_point": "Finding the Matrix Representation of an Affine Transformation Given its Parametric Form",
    "problem": "The matrix form of the affine transformation\n\n$$\nx=-5v-2,\\,y=7v-2u-3\n$$\n\nis shown below. What is the value of $a+b+c?$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & a \\\\ -2 & b\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}c \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
    "worked_solution": "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nFirst, notice that we can express the given transformation as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSeparating the constants and expressing the linear part as a product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v-2 \\\\ 7v-2u-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5v \\\\ -2u+7v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-5+7+(-2)=0.\n$$",
